{
  "structure_templates_version": "1",
  "note": "Named song structures as data. A template is a contract, not a label: the lyric generator is handed it as a writing brief, the composer instantiates its bar plan, and check_lyrics.py verifies the result against it. Sections are listed one entry per occurrence, in performance order, so sequence checking is a straight comparison.",
  "default_syllable_band": [
    6,
    10
  ],
  "assumptions": "Bar counts assume 4/4 and are the conventional shape for the form, not a law. Section bar counts at 8 and connective sections at 4 are the norm; a template's total bars divided by its tempo gives its duration, which is arithmetic and therefore belongs in code.",
